{title: Pass Me Not, O Gentle Saviour}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby / William H. Doane}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: F}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}
{score: pass-me-not-o-gentle-saviour.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Pass me not, O gentle [Bb]Saviour
[F]Hear my humble [C7]cry
While on [F]others Thou art [Bb]calling
[F]Do not pass me [C7]by[F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Saviour, Saviour
[Bb]Hear my humble [F]cry
While on [F]others Thou art [Bb]calling
[F]Do not pass me [C7]by[F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Let me at a throne of [Bb]mercy
[F]Find a sweet re[C7]lief
[F]Kneeling there in deep con[Bb]trition
[F]Help my un[C7]belief[F]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Trusting only in Thy [Bb]merit
[F]Would I seek Thy [C7]face
[F]Heal my wounded, broken [Bb]spirit
[F]Save me by Thy [C7]grace[F]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Thou the spring of all my [Bb]comfort
[F]More than life to [C7]me
[F]Whom have I on earth be[Bb]side Thee?
[F]Whom in heaven but [C7]Thee?[F]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
